  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The way movement and radial menu navigation works when you're using hand tracking (where you have to move your hand to move and rotate) could actually be a great option for users that have severe stick drift, but who still prefer to use controllers, if it was retooled to work with them. \n\nControllers can be tracked with far greater precision and control and can feel a lot more responsive than hand tracking.\n\nImagine pressing a button, or clicking in a useless joystick and moving your controller around like a flight stick the same way you would with hand tracking.",
